sec.p:
Finally, the RPL objective is not the only possible implementation of a JEPA given our three-component network architecture. Alternatively, one could also optimize the same network for predicting future representations ct+Δ from the integrator instead of zt+Δ, yielding the context-predictive learning (CL) objective function:
(6)
LCL=‖f(ct)−SG(ct+Δ)‖2. \begin{document}$$\displaystyle \begin{equation*} \mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{CL}}=\left\|f\left(\boldsymbol{c}_{t}\right)-\mathrm{SG}\left(\boldsymbol{c}_{t+\Delta}\right)\right\|^{2} . \tag{6} \end{equation*}$$\end{document}
